# Shared
NODE_ENV=development
LOG_LEVEL=info

# Kafka — one hosted cluster shared by the team (ADR-0008, decision note of
# 2026-10-02). No broker runs on anyone's laptop. Until the cutover on
# 13 Oct 2026 this is Aiven's free plan; after it, Confluent Cloud, and only
# this block changes. Check it with `npm run kafka:check`.
# Get the values from a teammate by password manager or private message, never
# git, Jira or the team channel.
#
# KAFKA_BROKERS: Aiven console → service → Connection information, with the
#   authentication method set to SASL (its port differs from the certificate one).
# KAFKA_SASL_MECHANISM: plain, scram-sha-256 or scram-sha-512. Aiven uses
#   scram-sha-256; Confluent uses plain, with an API key and secret.
KAFKA_BROKERS=replace-with-bootstrap-server:port
KAFKA_SASL_MECHANISM=scram-sha-256
KAFKA_SASL_USERNAME=replace-with-kafka-username-or-api-key
KAFKA_SASL_PASSWORD=replace-with-kafka-password-or-api-secret
# KAFKA_SSL_CA_PATH: Aiven signs its brokers with its own project CA, so
#   download ca.pem from Connection information and point at it here. Keep it
#   OUTSIDE the repo; ~ means your home folder. Leave empty for Confluent,
#   whose certificates are publicly trusted.
KAFKA_SSL_CA_PATH=~/.connectsphere/kafka/ca.pem
#
# Consumer groups: a deployed consumer joins `connectsphere.<service>.<consumer>`,
# e.g. connectsphere.notification.event-notifier. On a laptop the group gets
# `.<KAFKA_GROUP_SUFFIX>` appended, e.g. connectsphere.notification.event-notifier.dev-sk,
# so your local consumer never takes partitions from the deployed one or a
# teammate's. Set it to dev-<your initials>; leave it empty only in deployed
# environments. Topics are shared: there are no per-person topics.
KAFKA_GROUP_SUFFIX=dev-replace-with-your-initials

# Supabase (shared by every service) — the team's hosted project.
# DATABASE_URL: dashboard → Connect → Transaction pooler (port 6543). That
# pooler does not support prepared statements, so connect with prepare: false.
DATABASE_URL=replace-with-transaction-pooler-connection-string
SUPABASE_URL=https://replace-with-project-ref.supabase.co
SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=replace-with-anon-key-from-project-settings
SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=replace-with-service-role-key-from-project-settings
SUPABASE_JWKS_URL=https://replace-with-project-ref.supabase.co/auth/v1/.well-known/jwks.json
INTERNAL_TOKEN_SECRET=replace-with-a-long-random-string

# planning-core — the one staff-facing deployable (ADR-0004): the identity,
# event, venue, equipment and change modules in one process. Older .env files
# may still set PORT, SERVICE_NAME, DATABASE_SCHEMA, EVENT_PORT,
# EVENT_DATABASE_SCHEMA and IDENTITY_BASE_URL for the two services it replaced;
# nothing reads them any more, so they can be deleted.
PLANNING_CORE_PORT=8090

# Notification service (EN-04.3, ADR-0008): consumes connectsphere.event.v1 and
# stores T2's notifications in the notification schema. `npm run dev` starts it.
# Its consumer groups follow the rule above: connectsphere.notification.event-notifier
# and connectsphere.notification.retry-worker, plus .<KAFKA_GROUP_SUFFIX> on a laptop.
# Without KAFKA_* it serves /healthz and /readyz but creates no notifications.
NOTIFICATION_PORT=8091
# T2: the notification service asks planning-core who a token belongs to
# (GET /api/v1/users/me). Defaults to http://127.0.0.1:<PLANNING_CORE_PORT>; set it
# only when planning-core runs elsewhere.
# PLANNING_CORE_URL=

# Event module
# EVENT_SERVICE_NAME is no longer read: since EN-04.2 the event module's
# messages are CloudEvents with the fixed source /connectsphere/planning-core/event.
# TODO(E1/E2): the eligible coordinator pool is configuration while automatic
# assignment and nominee eligibility are stubbed. Comma-separated
# identity.users.id values. Replace with a lookup of active EVENT_COORDINATOR
# users through the identity module when E1/E2 are built for real.
# Both seeded coordinators (tests/README.md) are listed so the round-robin
# (E1) and reassignment (E2) test cases have a second coordinator to use.
EVENT_COORDINATOR_POOL=00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000002,00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000008
